Hoàng Mai Mobile lists "Camera" among its products and components [Data: Sources (8, 10, 18, 35, 27, +more)]. For newly purchased items, the company has a warranty policy in place.

To be eligible for warranty, a product must meet several conditions: it must have a technical fault originating from the manufacturer, remain in its original state without structural changes, be within the specified warranty period, and have intact warranty stamps from Hoàng Mai Mobile [Data: Sources (10, 18)].

However, there are specific situations where a product will not be covered under warranty. These include damage caused by incorrect usage, wrong voltage, or incorrect technical specifications, as well as damage from drops or impacts. Products that have been tampered with or repaired by entities other than Hoàng Mai Mobile are also excluded. Furthermore, items with missing, torn, faded, or counterfeit warranty stamps, or those affected by water, short circuits, oxidation, or deformation, will not be accepted for warranty claims. Products that have exceeded their stated warranty period are also ineligible [Data: Sources (10, 18)].

While the data lists "Camera" as a product, specific warranty durations for cameras are not detailed. The most specific warranty information provided is for "Màn hình – Cảm ứng" (Screen – Touchscreen), which offers a 6-month warranty for touch functionality (provided it still displays, has no scratches or cracks, and a straight cable). Roger screens also have a 6-month storage warranty covering issues like detached seals, air bubbles, unresponsive touch, flickering, image retention, or lines [Data: Sources (10, 18)]. For precise warranty details regarding a newly purchased camera, it would be advisable to consult the specific purchase documentation or contact Hoàng Mai Mobile directly.


