Hoàng Mai Mobile outlines a clear and comprehensive policy for shipping, delivery, and goods inspection to ensure customer satisfaction and transparency.

**Shipping and Delivery Methods**
Hoàng Mai Mobile offers two primary delivery methods: direct purchase at their store located at 08 ngõ 117 phố Thái Hà, phường Trung Liệt, quận Đống Đa, TP. Hà Nội, or nationwide delivery (ship hàng) through reputable shipping partners [Data: Sources (1)]. Orders are typically confirmed and processed within 2 hours of receiving information, with an estimated delivery time of 2-4 days, depending on the geographical location or specific agreements made during the order process [Data: Sources (1)]. Potential delays can occur due to inability to contact the customer, inaccurate addresses, sudden increases in order volume, or issues with shipping partners [Data: Sources (1)]. Shipping fees are calculated based on the third-party shipping unit's rates and will be communicated during order confirmation [Data: Sources (1)]. The company delivers nationwide, and for provincial customers, wholesale orders, or large quantities, delivery can be arranged via bus companies or transport companies as agreed upon, with specific fees provided [Data: Sources (1)].

**Order Packaging and Responsibility**
All orders are packaged and sealed intact before shipment, with complete recipient information and a tracking code on each package [Data: Sources (1, 2)]. Orders may include a warehouse release slip or financial invoice, which serves as proof of value and for handling complaints [Data: Sources (1, 2)]. Hoàng Mai Mobile takes direct responsibility for resolving issues with customers if products are damaged during transit, even if caused by a third-party carrier [Data: Sources (2)]. Customers have the right to refuse damaged goods and request an exchange or return according to the "return for refund" policy [Data: Sources (2)]. In cases of delivery delays, Hoàng Mai Mobile will proactively contact the customer, who can then choose to wait or cancel the order [Data: Sources (2)].

**Goods Inspection Policy**
Customers are entitled to open and inspect the product package before payment to ensure the correct model, quantity, and condition as per the order [Data: Sources (2)]. However, customers are not permitted to test or use the product during inspection [Data: Sources (2)]. If the product meets expectations, the customer proceeds with payment. If not satisfied, the customer can refuse to accept the goods and will be responsible for a return fee equivalent to the initial shipping cost [Data: Sources (2)]. Delivery personnel are required to wait for the customer to inspect the goods; if they refuse, customers should contact the hotline at 0982.15.3333 for support [Data: Sources (2)]. It is crucial not to use sharp objects to open packages to avoid damaging the product, as damage caused by the recipient will not be eligible for exchange, return, or warranty [Data: Sources (2)].

**Mandatory Notes for Receiving Goods**
Upon receiving an order, customers must record a video of the entire unboxing and product testing process, capturing all angles and the product's condition [Data: Sources (2)]. If the product is found to be broken, has torn cables, or broken sockets, Hoàng Mai Mobile must be notified within 24 hours of receipt [Data: Sources (2)]. Claims made after 24 hours will not be the responsibility of Hoàng Mai Mobile [Data: Sources (2)]. All outgoing products are thoroughly checked under internal surveillance cameras, so customers must provide video evidence for any shipping-related damage claims [Data: Sources (2)]. Hoàng Mai Mobile commits to timely delivery, secure packaging, safe delivery, and protecting customer rights [Data: Sources (2)].


